    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 261,
        "text": "Hi everyone, thanks for coming to the debate club meeting. Today we need to plan our argument for the school debate next month. The topic is 'Students should learn practical skills at school.' I think we should start with a clear topic sentence. Any ideas?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "987db09c50e463a8c2422506cbb28938169dbd7b5a1554156d200ad10de3c6f4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 268,
        "sourceEnd": 411,
        "text": "Yes, I have one. 'Schools should teach practical skills because these skills help students in daily life.' That's a good topic sentence, right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "2d743e8020b80913b49a2e94d476fc7399c37eca263ad9e5aa7c93eda59ef7cf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 418,
        "sourceEnd": 661,
        "text": "That's a good start, Leo. But we need supporting sentences. For example, we can say that cooking and budgeting are useful for everyone. Although some students think these skills are not academic, they are very important for independent living.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "bd56e589fb86916a4153285999b281e5a6d45a9b5b60cffd425e8fd7a4ce5e24",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 668,
        "sourceEnd": 843,
        "text": "I agree. While academic subjects like math and science are important, practical skills are also necessary. For instance, knowing how to cook can save money and improve health.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "fdca25dd33c4686c5d23d9c959fbc9e1f84ee21bbe9d1a4b9c462b52ab6b3864",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 850,
        "sourceEnd": 1028,
        "text": "Exactly. And we should also mention that because of busy school schedules, many students don't have time to learn these skills at home. So school is the best place to teach them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "2b1f8d4564958fbb5c97c186d375ba23e0eef4dccb867f5a32233ae4146b055e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1035,
        "sourceEnd": 1252,
        "text": "That's a strong point. But wait, I think we should also consider the opposite view. Some people say that schools already have too many subjects. Because of this, adding practical skills might be too much for students.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "f72bd0a4a30a4aae4021068df2a2b3bd250131a88b462e27979cc973a31abed3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1259,
        "sourceEnd": 1467,
        "text": "Good point. But we can argue that practical skills can be integrated into existing subjects. For example, math classes can include budgeting exercises. Although it might require some planning, it is possible.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "6f001775ea297be1b2cfe411991ee21400fe9dd3720687d84d5d6ad7cef68cec",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1474,
        "sourceEnd": 1746,
        "text": "OK, so our argument structure could be: first, a topic sentence about the importance of practical skills. Then, supporting sentences with examples like cooking and budgeting. Finally, a conclusion that schools should teach these skills because they are essential for life.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "dab6b40d089e2c9bb599540a2ac482d98aa665159de0a894d7abfc1c86db5644",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1753,
        "sourceEnd": 2082,
        "text": "That sounds good. Let's also remember to use 'although' and 'while' to show contrast, and 'because' and 'because of' to show reasons. For example, 'Although some students prefer traditional subjects, practical skills are equally important.' And 'Because of the changing job market, students need practical skills more than ever.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "c059a21ce3745c9f4d2b792f9aef9e7130ace210d34d4a573b148934f691fcc3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2089,
        "sourceEnd": 2200,
        "text": "Nice. I'll write these down. So, our main argument is clear. Let's meet again next week to practice our speech.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "acdca7d113b5e2125a0c147516d7595ade67c94f05aa832c6cbc842b97887783",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2207,
        "sourceEnd": 2240,
        "text": "Great. Thanks, Leo. See you then.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "723a41a275d9cc671979cc50799f31eac7d636aa2c7da844379973b508969b6d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
